					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-261559#post-1572707</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-261559/running#post-1572707</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Mon, 24 Sep 2012 23:21:55 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Enma Ai</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>500266</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>'Tis true the ending makes no sense if you don't know that this is a <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-966">SCP-966</a> story; this was pretty much written to show how one of their victims would feel. The death seemingly coming out of nowhere was intencional, since there's no way the person would be able to detect 966.</p> <p>If you don't mind, I'd like to know which italicized parts you found badly placed.</p> <p>Can't do much about your distate for the second person writing, though :P</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-261559#post-1571729</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-261559/running#post-1571729</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Sun, 23 Sep 2012 18:32:17 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Circle Breaker</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1364455</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <blockquote> <p>you see a large piece of your flesh being ripped <strong>of</strong> your body</p> </blockquote> <p>My mastery of the English language isn't great, but shouldn't that be &quot;ripped <strong>off</strong> your body&quot;?</p> <p>While it isn't bad, I didn't really feel a sense of foreboding or tension. I mean, it was pretty clear he whatever he was running from was going to catch up. I also have to agree with TL333s here, not a huge fan of the second person point of view.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
